/target/
/artifacts/
/coverage/
/.fuzz-target-lock

# `corpus/` is deliberately NOT ignored. Seeds are how a finding stays replayable: a corpus that lives
# only in a developer's working tree cannot reproduce a crash for anyone else.
#
# Only three hand-written seeds are committed. A first run from an empty corpus makes libFuzzer emit
# several hundred coverage-increasing entries — that is convergence, not signal, and it will be
# regenerated by the next run. Commit the corpus when it holds something a reviewer can read.
#
# `artifacts/` is ignored because it is empty until something crashes. When it stops being empty, that
# is a finding: un-ignore it and commit the reproducer in the same change that fixes the bug.